{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.FrechetShohat","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FrechetShohat","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.ProbabilityMeasure","lean:module:Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.FiniteMeasureExt","lean:module:Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.ExpDecay","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Gamma.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FrechetShohat.FrechetShohatStieltjes.tendsto_of_moments","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FrechetShohat.FrechetShohatStieltjes.tendsto_of_moments","kind":"theorem","line":250,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FrechetShohat.lean#L250-L250","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FrechetShohat.FrechetShohatStieltjes.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FrechetShohat.FrechetShohatStieltjes.mk","kind":"ctor","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FrechetShohat.lean#L249-L249","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FrechetShohat.FrechetShohatStieltjes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FrechetShohat.FrechetShohatStieltjes","kind":"class","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FrechetShohat.lean#L236-L258","doc":"**Fréchet–Shohat / method of moments (classical theorem, Mathlib\ngap), Stieltjes form with an explicit limit candidate.** If probability\nmeasures `μs n`, all supported on `[0,∞)` with all moments finite, have\n`k`-th moments converging to `M k` for every `k`, and `μ` realizes the\nmoment data `M`, and `M` is Stieltjes-determinate, then `μs → μ` in the\ntopology of weak convergence. Fréchet–Shohat, Trans. AMS 33 (1931)\n533–543; Billingsley, *Probability and Measure*, 3rd ed., Thm. 30.2.\nThe uniqueness half is already provable\n(`tendsto_probabilityMeasure_unique`); the convergence half needs\ntightness-from-moments + Prokhorov/Helly selection, absent from the\npinned Mathlib.\n\nTODO upstream: `Mathlib.Probability.MomentProblem` (new file). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FrechetShohat.CarlemanDeterminacyStieltjes.determinate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FrechetShohat.CarlemanDeterminacyStieltjes.determinate","kind":"theorem","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FrechetShohat.lean#L233-L233","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FrechetShohat.CarlemanDeterminacyStieltjes.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FrechetShohat.CarlemanDeterminacyStieltjes.mk","kind":"ctor","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FrechetShohat.lean#L232-L232","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FrechetShohat.CarlemanDeterminacyStieltjes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FrechetShohat.CarlemanDeterminacyStieltjes","kind":"class","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FrechetShohat.lean#L223-L234","doc":"**Carleman–Stieltjes determinacy (classical theorem, Mathlib gap).**\nIf the moment sequence `M` (of genuine Stieltjes moment data, positive)\nsatisfies the Carleman condition `Σ_k M_k^{−1/(2k)} = ∞`, the Stieltjes\nmoment problem for `M` is determinate. Simon, Adv. Math. 137 (1998)\n82–203, Cor. 4.5 / Thm. 5.14; Akhiezer, *The Classical Moment Problem*,\n1965. `QOU.Archimedean.BorelProperTimeMoment.carleman_divergence` proves\nthe hypothesis for `M k = k!`; this class carries the theorem itself.\n\nTODO upstream: `Mathlib.Probability.MomentProblem` (new file). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FrechetShohat.tendsto_probabilityMeasure_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FrechetShohat.tendsto_probabilityMeasure_unique","kind":"theorem","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FrechetShohat.lean#L192-L209","doc":"**Weak limits of probability measures on `ℝ` are unique.** Two weak\nlimits of the same net integrate every bounded continuous function\nidentically (`tendsto_nhds_unique` in `ℝ`), hence coincide by\n`ext_of_forall_integral_eq_of_IsFiniteMeasure`. This is the uniqueness\nhalf of the Fréchet–Shohat conclusion; only the *existence/convergence*\nhalf remains a Mathlib gap.\n\nTODO upstream: `Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.ProbabilityMeasure` — a\n`T2Space (ProbabilityMeasure ℝ)` instance would subsume this. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FrechetShohat.hasStieltjesMoments_schwinger","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FrechetShohat.hasStieltjesMoments_schwinger","kind":"theorem","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FrechetShohat.lean#L182-L187","doc":"The Schwinger measure realizes the factorial Stieltjes moment data —\nthe `HasStieltjesMoments` package, fully proved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FrechetShohat.integral_pow_schwingerMeasure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FrechetShohat.integral_pow_schwingerMeasure","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FrechetShohat.lean#L164-L180","doc":"**The factorial moments (proved).** The `k`-th moment of the unit\nSchwinger measure is `k!`: `∫ s^k · e^{−s} ds = Γ(k+1) = k!`. Together\nwith `QOU.Archimedean.BorelProperTimeMoment.moment_eq_factorial` (the\n`ds/s`-shifted form) this is the moment-data leg of the balanced-kernel\nconvergence theorem. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FrechetShohat.integrable_pow_schwingerMeasure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FrechetShohat.integrable_pow_schwingerMeasure","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FrechetShohat.lean#L149-L162","doc":"Every monomial is integrable against the Schwinger measure\n(the Gamma integral converges). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FrechetShohat.schwingerProbabilityMeasure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FrechetShohat.schwingerProbabilityMeasure","kind":"def","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FrechetShohat.lean#L143-L147","doc":"The Schwinger measure as a bundled probability measure on `ℝ` —\nthe weak-convergence limit object of the balanced q-Borel kernel\nfamily. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FrechetShohat.instIsProbabilityMeasureRealSchwingerMeasure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FrechetShohat.instIsProbabilityMeasureRealSchwingerMeasure","kind":"instance","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FrechetShohat.lean#L141-L141","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FrechetShohat.schwingerMeasure_univ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FrechetShohat.schwingerMeasure_univ","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FrechetShohat.lean#L127-L139","doc":"Total mass one: `∫₀^∞ e^{−s} ds = Γ(1) = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FrechetShohat.schwingerMeasure_Iio_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FrechetShohat.schwingerMeasure_Iio_zero","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FrechetShohat.lean#L121-L125","doc":"The Schwinger measure carries no mass left of the origin. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FrechetShohat.schwingerMeasure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FrechetShohat.schwingerMeasure","kind":"def","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FrechetShohat.lean#L107-L111","doc":"The unit Schwinger (proper-time) measure `e^{−s}·ds` on `(0,∞)`,\nas a Borel measure on `ℝ`. Coincides with the rate-1 exponential\ndistribution `ProbabilityTheory.expMeasure 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FrechetShohat.CarlemanCondition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FrechetShohat.CarlemanCondition","kind":"def","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FrechetShohat.lean#L97-L103","doc":"`CarlemanCondition M`: the Carleman series `Σ_k M_k^{−1/(2k)}`\ndiverges (stated as non-summability, matching\n`QOU.Archimedean.BorelProperTimeMoment.carleman_divergence`, which\nproves exactly this for `M k = k!`). The `k = 0` term is the harmless\nconstant `M 0 ^ 0 = 1` under Lean's `1/0 = 0` convention. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FrechetShohat.StieltjesDeterminate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FrechetShohat.StieltjesDeterminate","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FrechetShohat.lean#L90-L95","doc":"`StieltjesDeterminate M`: at most one probability measure on `ℝ`\nsupported on `[0,∞)` has moment sequence `M` — the *determinacy*\nproperty of the Stieltjes moment problem. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FrechetShohat.HasStieltjesMoments","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FrechetShohat.HasStieltjesMoments","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FrechetShohat.lean#L82-L88","doc":"`HasStieltjesMoments μ M`: the measure `μ` on `ℝ` is supported on\n`[0,∞)` (no mass on `Iio 0`), every monomial `s^k` is integrable, and the\n`k`-th moment is `M k`. This is the Stieltjes-side moment-data predicate\nof the classical moment problem. ","signatureChunk":0}]}